## F8 — Scaffold placeholders are unhelpfully generic

**Severity: low.**

The generated `tasks.md` row is:

```
| T1 | builder | internal/example.go | | sample/Requirement: <requirement> | `<verification>` | <acceptance> |
```

`internal/example.go` and `sample/Requirement:` are Go-project idioms in a
harness that is language-agnostic. In a PHP repository they read as noise. More
importantly the row demonstrates none of the format's actual rules: no multiple
values, so no separator; no dependency, so no id format; no real verification
command shape.

### Suggested fix

A two-row scaffold demonstrating multi-value cells and a dependency edge teaches
the entire format in the place the author is already looking:

```
| T1 | builder | src/a.php; src/b.php | | cap/Requirement: One; cap/Requirement: Two | `make test` | Observable result. |
| T2 | builder | src/c.php | T1 | cap/Requirement: Three | `make lint` | Observable result. |
```

